A. THIRD-PARTY SOURCE DISTRIBUTED IN THIS REPOSITORY
---------------------------------------------------
  None.

  The official FOMO26 container validator used to be vendored here, 84 files under
  third_party/fomo26_container_validator/. It has been removed. Its upstream declares no
  licence, and shipping it inside a public release would have been redistribution on
  undefined terms -- the one thing a source-only release cannot argue away.

  What remains is our own record, not upstream's code:
    finetuning/container/validator_manifest.json   paths + digests of the pinned commit
    finetuning/container/official_contract.json    the task interface, as data

  The validator is an external tool. Acquiring and running it is the reader's own act under
  whatever terms upstream offers; nothing here grants any right to it. It is fetched
  explicitly (release.py validator acquire), only ever at the pinned commit
  d442af2e9bdade58be20c2ee0cbabf8d0439e32b, and verified against the manifest before use.
  Its absence is an error, never a pass.

