C. CONTAINER IMAGES
-------------------
A built SIF redistributes its installed packages as binaries, which is a different act from
publishing this source. Any image built from this repository needs its own NOTICE covering
what it actually contains; see finetuning/container/historical_sif_profile.json for the
submitted image's dependency set.

STATUS: SOURCE-RELEASE APPROVED BY THE PROJECT OWNER
---------------------------------------------------
The project owner has approved publication under this source-only scope. That is an owner's
release decision, not legal-counsel review: this file is assembled from package metadata and
lock evidence, metadata is preliminary evidence and not legal certainty, and nothing here
constitutes a legal opinion.

The blocking item is resolved by removal rather than by argument -- no validator source is
redistributed. One item stays open and is deliberately out of scope for a source release:
colorama's licence is unresolved in the recorded metadata, and it is not in the runtime
